# High Country AI guidance

Canonical state lives in `.ai/`. Read `.ai/STATE.json` when campaign continuity matters, `.ai/REQUIREMENTS.md` for requirement or harness changes, and `.ai/ROUTING.md` only for model routing or escalation. HANDOFF and history are retrieval-only. Do not load all three merely because a task is large.

Work from the requested outcome and hard constraints. Choose proportionate investigation and verification; do not automatically chain every measurement, capture, grading, critic, or second-pass workflow. Broaden only when scope, risk, or evidence warrants it.

Use Scout (Luna), Worker (Terra), Senior (Sol), and Expert (Astra) through the installed router when delegation adds value. Astra is a fresh, compact decision-only escalation, not the default coding model.
